<h2 class="wp-block-heading">More Sweet Potato Recipes&nbsp;</h2>



<p>If you are like me and can&rsquo;t get enough of sweet potatoes, here are a few more recipes I make every year around the holidays:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>My adaptation of Trisha Yearwood&rsquo;s <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/sweet-potato-souffle/">Sweet Potato Souffl&eacute; Recipe</a> has been one of the most popular <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/holiday-potato-recipes/">holiday potato recipes</a> on the blog, thanks to its thick butter and pecan streusel-like topping.</li>



<li>If you&rsquo;re looking for something both sweet and savory, try my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/sweet-potato-stacks/">Sweet Potato Stacks</a>. It&rsquo;s baked thin slices of sweet potatoes that are perfect for brunch, dinner, or any holiday meal.</li>



<li>And if you&rsquo;re craving something warm and comforting, this <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/vegan-sweet-potato-soup/">Vegan Sweet Potato Soup</a> is silky, spiced with ginger and carrots, and perfect as either a holiday starter or a simple weeknight meal.</li>
</ul>
